            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jillian"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Very nice salad! I thinly sliced the cucumber and added the salt. I let that set for about twenty minutes to let the cucumbers produce their own water. I added thin sliced red onion, cut the amount of sugar in half, used white wine vinegar, left the amount of dill the same and omitted the water. I chilled it for the time stated and it went great with grilled chicken. If you like this, you'll like \"Dilly Cucumber Salad\" from this site."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Nadine"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I prepared the recipe for a potluck and everyone loved it! I had reviewed the comments of others and made the following modifications: sprinkled salt on the sliced cucumbers and let sit for 20 mins, didn’t add water as plenty of liquid seeped from the cucumbers, used fresh dill, and cut sugar quantity’s in half.",
            "datePublished": "2018-09-11T13:25:41.340Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Carnivore"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I incorporated suggestions by others: brown rice vinegar, skipped water (ABSOLUTELY - the cukes weep more than enough fluid !!!), reduced to 2/3 C sugar and later 1/2). Radically increased dill to 3 T dry on second pass and will use finely-chopped fresh the next time. Used a mandoline to add render a red Bell pepper into 1.5mm slivers of color and doubled the onion, using Vidalias. \n\nOK, it is entirely appropriate for my nick to be \"Carnivore\" . . . yet I made a meal out of this salad two nights running.",
            "datePublished": "2011-06-03T02:13:17.130Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
